<section class="section">
  <div class="container" style="max-width:820px">
    <div class="text-center" style="margin-bottom:2rem">
      <span class="section-label">Timeline</span>
      <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-inline:auto">The whole process, end to end</h2>
    </div>

    <ol class="timeline">
      <li class="timeline-item">
        <span class="timeline-time">Optional &middot; 20 to 30 minutes</span>
        <h3>Discovery call</h3>
        <p>The call is free and optional; you can sign up without one. We talk on Google Meet, you tell me what you do, and I work out what the site needs to do for you. If I'm not the right fit, I'll tell you on the call.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>What you do and who you serve</li>
          <li>What's working, or not, on your current site</li>
          <li>What the new site should bring in: phone calls, booked jobs, or quote requests</li>
          <li>Your timeline, the content you have, and your questions</li>
        </ul>
      </li>

      <li class="timeline-item">
        <span class="timeline-time">Day 1&ndash;2 &middot; Agreement and kickoff</span>
        <h3>Service agreement and first payment</h3>
        <p>You sign the plain-English service agreement and make your first monthly payment. Work begins when that payment clears, with no large deposit up front.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Service agreement signed online</li>
          <li>First monthly payment processed securely</li>
          <li>Shared folder for your logo, photos, and other content</li>
          <li>Design under way once your payment clears</li>
        </ul>
      </li>

      <li class="timeline-item">
        <span class="timeline-time">Week 1&ndash;2 &middot; 7&ndash;10 business days</span>
        <h3>Design and build</h3>
        <p>I write every line of code from scratch for your brand. Within the first few days you get a live preview link, so you can give feedback while the work is moving. Ask for as many revisions as you need, because I don't charge per change. The rounds after the first draft are where most of the work that brings in calls gets done.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Design made for your industry and services</li>
          <li>Custom code, written from scratch</li>
          <li>A live preview link to share with your team</li>
          <li>Unlimited revisions until you're happy</li>
        </ul>
      </li>

      <li class="timeline-item">
        <span class="timeline-time">Week 2&ndash;3 &middot; Launch day</span>
        <h3>Launch</h3>
        <p>I point your domain at the hosting, check that everything works, submit your sitemap to Google and Bing, and email you a plain-English owner's guide. You don't touch anything technical.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Domain connected and security certificate (SSL) switched on</li>
          <li>Sitemap submitted to Google and Bing</li>
          <li>Business details for Google (local-business schema) checked</li>
          <li>Owner's guide emailed to you</li>
        </ul>
      </li>

      <li class="timeline-item">
        <span class="timeline-time">Ongoing &middot; For as long as you're with me</span>
        <h3>Updates and support</h3>
        <p>After launch, I stay with the work. When something changes, such as new hours, a new service, or a seasonal promotion, email or text me, and the change goes live quickly on most business days. I also watch your site's uptime, speed, security, and links.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Unlimited content updates on the monthly plan</li>
          <li>Direct access to me for anything urgent</li>
          <li>Security, uptime, and Google speed scores monitored</li>
          <li>A quarterly check-in on what's working and what to add</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

