<section class="section">
  <div class="container text-center" style="max-width:720px">
    <span class="section-label">Process FAQ</span>
    <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-inline:auto">Common process questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What if I don't have content yet? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">I write it for you. I draft the copy in your voice from what you tell me on the call or in the onboarding form. Then we revise it together until each page sounds the way you talk to customers.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">Can I see the site while you're building it? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">Yes, and you should. I share a live preview link early in the build, and you can forward it to anyone whose opinion you want. You see the work from start to finish.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">How many rounds of revisions do I get? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">As many as you need. I don't charge by the change, and I don't rush the rounds. I'd rather you be happy before launch than find something to fix the day after.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What if I already have a domain? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">That's the most common case. The domain stays registered in your name at your registrar, and on launch day I point it at the new hosting, so you never have to touch it.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-btn" aria-expanded="false">What happens to my old website? <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">I time the switch so there's no downtime between the two sites. Once the new one is live, you can take the old one down or keep a private archive.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

